```css
body {
  font-size: 24px;
}
```
This will set the font size to 24 pixels.  You can also use other units like “em” or “rem”, which will make the font size relative to the current font size.  For example, you could use “em” to make the font size twice as large as the current font size:
```css
body {
  font-size: 2em;
}
```

